Everything from YAML (kept)
description: the surface you know - block and flow, scalars, comments, the odd corners too
- 'yamlover keeps the YAML surface you know:'
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Feature
    - Example
      width: 2
  - ['Block mappings & sequences', '`key: value` / `- item`']
  - ['Flow style (one line, or spanning them - see concretes)', '`{a: 1, b: 2}`, `[1, 2, 3]`']
  - ['A flow token as a KEY', '`{[1, 2]: 3}`, and `[256, 256]: *thumb` in block - the key is that text']
  - [Comments, '`# note`']
  - ['Scalars (plain / quoted / folded / literal)', '`a`, `''a''`, `"a"`, `>`, `|`']
  - ['`null` spellings, incl. `~` in value position', '`key: ~` → null']
  - ['Float specials (YAML, **not** json5''s `Infinity`/`NaN`)', '`.inf`, `-.inf`, `.nan` (case-tolerant: `.Inf`/`.NaN`)']
  - ['`&` anchors and `*` aliases', '`&a {...}` ... `*a` - syntax kept, **meaning extended**']
- >
  A YAML `- item` sequence entry is the same thing as a keyless entry in the one ordered container -
  an entry with no string key ([order is data](::language:principles:order-is-data)).
